  "schoolyard_use_notes": "This tree has narrow, needle-like leaves that can be used to discuss leaf structure and water conservation in plants. The bark peels off in paper-like sheets, providing a tactile experience for students and a lesson in plant adaptation. It produces fluffy white flowers that can attract pollinators, making it useful for lessons on plant reproduction and ecosystems. The tree's resilience to drought conditions offers practical examples of survival strategies in harsh environments.",
